There is no mathematics on this page. Folio 72v is a household linen inventory in German Kurrent script. It lists pieces (Stück) and remnants (Reste) of cloth, measured in Ellen (ells).

The page has three parts:

(a) Top left, in pencil, every line ticked with '+': 26 Ellen of fine (home-spun?) linen; 45 Ellen; 20 Ellen self-spun linen; 3 remnants of 20 Ellen self-spun linen each; 1 linen remnant of 13 Ellen; 1 linen remnant of 8 Ellen.

(b) Lower left, in ink, a fuller master list:
- 7 pieces of house-made linen at 60 Ellen each;
- 5 remnants at 20, 2 remnants at 13, 1 remnant at 8;
- 1 remnant of 'gewirktes'(?) linen at 8 1/2;
- 3 remnants of finer linen at 26, 45 and 20;
- 1 piece of Bielefeld factory linen at 54 Ellen;
- 2 pieces of (finer?) kitchen-towel drill at 40 and 29;
- 1 piece of blue-and-white checked linen (the word 'Bettlaken-' is struck out), 30 Ellen; a further 20 Ellen;
- 1 unwashed damask table set, 5 1/2 Ellen;
- 3 pieces of table drill at 20, 29 and 10 Ellen;
- 4 unwashed napkins;
- 2 pieces of drill for hand towels at 4 and 7 Ellen.

(c) Right column, in pencil, mostly ticked '+'. This is a checklist that re-enumerates the same items one by one: 7 pieces at 60; Bielefeld 54; the damask set (20 Ellen and 5 1/2 Ellen); 20 Ellen of self-spun drill for napkins; 29 and 10 Ellen of drill for tablecloths; 4 and 7 Ellen of drill for towels; 4 napkins; an overwritten quantity of self-spun towel drill (probably the 40); 20, 13 and 8 1/2 Ellen of linen; 29 Ellen of kitchen-towel drill; 30 Ellen of bed-sheet linen; 20 Ellen of fine self-spun linen.

The ticks suggest the inventory was being checked against physical goods, perhaps when packing or unpacking. The next page carries Italian shipping and lodging notes (Fratelli Romagni in Marseille, Compagnia Valéry, a Venetian-style address, floor plans). This fits Riemann's Italian sojourns of 1862–66, so the list was plausibly made for a household move or storage. The only 'computation' is implicit bookkeeping of lengths. The theta-function notes on the next page are unrelated to this page.
